{
  "text": " or high-intensity interval training. I'll give that seven out of ten. It's a wonderful motor exercise, good for the heart, good for cardiovascular conditioning. However, there's a very strong point of concern for patients who have called underlying cardiovascular diseases. So it has to be done under the supervision of an expert cardiologist. Or in order to avoid the higher incidence of mortality or mobility, it should be better avoided in patients who have got cardiovascular diseases. For normal patients to improve endurance and stamina, it is an excellent formula exercise. That's why I'm giving that 7 out of 10.",
